"""Mutants of the patch 0281 keep-phase event decode, link-down detector and event-buffer re-post (sweet_wlan_g2.h), appended to E_G2_ROWS of tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py.
Each row is ("E: name", [(old, new)]): an exact-string edit of the header, killed by shim/wlan_g2_host_test.c (K4 / 0281 blocks) or shim/wlan_g2_host_l25wl.h.
Patch 0282 (W-D6 boot B, the re-join) adds, besides ROWS entries for sweet_wlan_g2.h (backoff, the detector's re-join states):
  L25_ROWS  (clause, name, old, new) edits of shim/sweet_wlan_l25_hs.h (the state machine, the kept secrets, the EAPOL hook), merged into MUTANTS of tools/test_wlan_l25_mutants.py and killed by
            shim/wlan_l25_host_test.c through shim/wlan_l25_host_rj.h
  WL_ROWS   (clause, name, old, new) edits of shim/sweet_wlan_l25_wl.h (the seven new rows and their content checks), same runner, killed by shim/wlan_l25_wl_host_test.c (rj_rows)
  EN0_ROWS  (name, rule, old, new) edits of shim/wlan_en0.h (the EAPOL divert and the raw tx), merged into MUTANTS of tools/test_wlan_en0_mutants.py, killed by shim/wlan_en0_host_test.c (test_eapol)
Every pattern must occur exactly once in its header (the runners fail otherwise: no silent hole)."""


def _em(name, old, new):
    return ("E: " + name, [(old, new)])


